# Do not create `apiagent-kit/.env`.
#
# Configuration for this repo is centralised in the .env at the REPO ROOT
# (one directory up). Two reasons:
#
#   1. The Python bot loads the root .env via `dotenv.load_dotenv()`, which
#      puts every value into os.environ. apiagent-kit is launched from Python
#      as a child process and inherits that environment, so process.env is
#      already populated — a second file here would only be a way for the two
#      to disagree.
#
#   2. `FRED_API_KEY`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `SEC_EDGAR_CONTACT`,
#      `APIAGENT_UA_PRODUCT` and `APIAGENT_UA_URL` are all documented there,
#      in the apiagent-kit section. `METACULUS_API_TOKEN` is NOT set anywhere:
#      cli.ts derives it from the bot's own `METACULUS_TOKEN`, since they are
#      the same credential under two names.
#
# The `ask` and `tools` npm scripts read `../.env` directly, so running them by
# hand from this directory works too.
#
# Upstream note: this file replaces the one shipped with the kit. Everything
# under src/ is still a verbatim copy of upstream; only package.json's two
# script paths and this file were changed.
#
# LLM_BASE_URL / LLM_API_KEY / LLM_MODEL are NOT set for this project. They are
# read only by examples/ask.ts, which drives the kit's own `runAgent` loop. The
# forecasting bot calls the toolkit directly and supplies its own model.
